From: Emception maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] wasm assets: parse install prefix with target semantics

The WASM install prefix describes the Emscripten target filesystem, not the
native bootstrap host. pathlib.Path turns /usr into the current drive's usr
directory on Windows, so derive the relative asset path with POSIX semantics.
---
 Tools/wasm/wasm_assets.py | 6 +++---
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Tools/wasm/wasm_assets.py b/Tools/wasm/wasm_assets.py
--- a/Tools/wasm/wasm_assets.py
+++ b/Tools/wasm/wasm_assets.py
@@ -195,2 +195,2 @@
-    default=pathlib.Path("/usr/local"),
-    type=path,
+    default=pathlib.PurePosixPath("/usr/local"),
+    type=pathlib.PurePosixPath,
@@ -203 +203 @@
-    relative_prefix = args.prefix.relative_to(pathlib.Path("/"))
+    relative_prefix = args.prefix.relative_to(pathlib.PurePosixPath("/"))
